{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of November 6, 2026:\n\n- **Read the fund’s notices and prospectus supplements.** They specify account requirements, transfer procedures, deadlines and any transaction blackout. There is no universal timetable.\n- **Arrange brokerage access.** If your direct account cannot hold ETFs, open an ETF-capable brokerage account and confirm it accepts the shares. Follow instructions to transfer mutual-fund shares before conversion or receive/transfer ETF shares afterward, if permitted.\n- **Check missed-deadline consequences.** Depending on the fund’s terms, shares might remain with a transfer agent, unable to be traded there until transferred to a broker, or be redeemed. Confirm delivery and trading availability; don’t assume immediate access.\n- **Check fractional-share treatment.** Fractions commonly are redeemed for cash, potentially realizing taxable gains or losses in taxable accounts.\n\n**Worth knowing:** A whole-fund conversion replaces mutual-fund shares with ETF shares. Adding an ETF share class alone does not automatically convert existing holdings."}}
